---
title: Frijoles con veneno
tags: [mexican, pork]
cuisine: mexican
source: Frijoles con Veneno by StarChefs, https://www.starchefs.com/recipes/frijoles-con-veneno
---

== Recado rojo ==

Bring a #pot{} of water to the boil. Add the @guajillo chiles{6}, @chiles de arbol{6}, @pasilla chiles{4} and @ancho chiles{4}, take it off the heat and leave until the chiles are soft.

Blend the chiles with the @garlic{8%cloves}(peeled), @ground oregano{1%tsp}, @ground cumin{1%tsp} and the juice of @orange{1} in a #blender{} until smooth, loosening with soaking liquid as needed. Sieve and refrigerate.

== Refried beans ==

Cook the @dried pinto beans{4%cups}(rinsed, soaked overnight) with the @garlic{8%cloves}(minced), @onion{1}(chopped) and @bay leaves{2} in a #stock pot{} over medium heat until tender. Season with @kosher salt{} and pull out the bay leaves.

Purée the beans in a #food processor{}.

Melt the @lard{2%cups} in a #heavy saucepan{} over medium heat, add the bean purée and heat through. Season again with @kosher salt{}.

== Pork ==

Season the @ground pork{} with @kosher salt{} and @ground black pepper{} and leave at room temperature ~{45%minutes}.

Melt the @lard{4%cups} in a #sauté pan{} over medium heat and brown the pork evenly.

Stir in as much recado rojo as you like and heat through. Add the juice of @orange{1} and season with more @kosher salt{} and @ground black pepper{}.

== Assembly ==

Spread the beans in a serving bowl and top with the pork. Finish with @pickled red onions{} and @queso fresco{}, and serve with @salsa{} and @flour tortillas{}.
